      09:27:03  received from agent (process 7004): update 6
      09:27:04  received from agent (process 7004): update 7
      09:27:04  received from helper: still running
   LangGraph says: run 01a17caf is running.

STEP 3. Stop 1, LangGraph's own stop: cancel the run (client.runs.cancel, the request LangGraph's client library sends).
   LangGraph says: run 01a17caf is interrupted.
   What the outside service receives, for 8 s:
      09:27:07  received from agent (process 7004): update 10
      09:27:08  received from agent (process 7004): update 11
      09:27:08  received from helper: still running
      09:27:09  received from agent (process 7004): update 12
      09:27:10  received from agent (process 7004): update 13
      09:27:10  received from helper: still running
      09:27:11  received from agent (process 7004): update 14
      09:27:12  received from agent (process 7004): update 15
      09:27:12  received from helper: still running
      09:27:13  received from agent (process 7004): update 16
      09:27:14  received from agent (process 7004): update 17
      09:27:14  received from helper: still running
   After the cancel the agent sent 8 more updates. The task is a plain (synchronous) function running in a thread of its own: the cancel stops LangGraph waiting for it, not the function, so it runs on while the run reads interrupted.

STEP 4. Stop 2: stop the server, as a developer presses Ctrl+C in its terminal.
   10 s later the server process is still running; pressing Ctrl+C again, as people do.
   20 s after the first Ctrl+C: the server no longer answers, but its process (7004) is still running.
   What the outside service receives, for 6 s:
      09:27:34  received from helper: still running
      09:27:34  received from agent (process 7004): update 37
      09:27:35  received from agent (process 7004): update 38
      09:27:36  received from helper: still running
      09:27:36  received from agent (process 7004): update 39
      09:27:37  received from agent (process 7004): update 40
      09:27:38  received from helper: still running
      09:27:38  received from agent (process 7004): update 41
      09:27:39  received from agent (process 7004): update 42
   Since the Ctrl+C the agent sent 25 updates (last: update 42). Ctrl+C makes the server stop taking requests, but Python does not let the process exit until the task's thread has finished, so the task runs on.

